IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- s 4B: the Act does not apply to a person in respect of whom a transitional approval or transitional licence mentioned in
-- section 66 of the Commodity Trading Act 1992 is in force, to the extent that the activities are regulated under, and authorised by, that section.
-- Imports prelude and daydate only.
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   Every defined term of s 2(1) is ONE function, named `s 2(1) "<term>" <the thing> is <the term>`, over the facts a person could state.
--   The result is MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--     JUST TRUE   the thing is within the term (a limb of the definition is met and no exclusion applies);
--     JUST FALSE  the TEXT says it is not: a definition that says "means" and no limb is met, or an express exclusion ("but does not include");
--     NOTHING     the text does not say: an "includes" definition (an open list) with no listed limb met.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--   Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "..."`; every branch that
--   answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
--   A limb the Act hands to the Authority, the regulations or another Act ("prescribed", "specified", "as defined in the
--   Banking Act 1970") is an INPUT named for the fact ("the Authority has prescribed ..."), never a thing read from memory.
--   The definitions apply "unless the context otherwise requires" (the chapeau of s 2(1)): that qualification is
--   `s 2(1) the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires` in sfa-definitions-rest.l4, not repeated here.

§ `s 4B: application`

-- src:4214 | 4B. This Act does not apply to a person in respect of whom a
-- src:4215 | transitional approval or transitional licence mentioned in section 66
-- src:4216 | of the Commodity Trading Act 1992 is in force, to the extent that the
-- src:4217 | activities carried out by the person are regulated under, and
-- src:4218 | authorised by, that section.
@ref s 4B (src:4214-4218)
GIVEN
    `a transitional approval or transitional licence mentioned in section 66 of the Commodity Trading Act 1992 is in force in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a transitional approval or transitional licence mentioned in section 66 of the Commodity Trading Act 1992 in force in respect of the person?
    `the activities carried out by the person are regulated under, and authorised by, that section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the activities the person carries out regulated under, and authorised by, section 66 of the Commodity Trading Act 1992?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4B this Act applies to the person in respect of the activities` MEANS
    IF `a transitional approval or transitional licence mentioned in section 66 of the Commodity Trading Act 1992 is in force in respect of the person` AND `the activities carried out by the person are regulated under, and authorised by, that section`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Act does not apply to a person in respect of whom a transitional approval or transitional licence mentioned in section 66 of the Commodity Trading Act 1992 is in force, to the extent that the activities carried out by the person are regulated under, and authorised by, that section"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent that the activities carried out by the person are regulated under, and authorised by, that section"; any other case is outside section 4B and this section says nothing about whether the Act applies
